From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:57:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/79] flashnext_mia: build module, kernel images and the
 TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE=mia selector

MiaAI-Lab's Flash Next (qwen4_exp) CUDA engine joins the build and the native CUDA server: her kernel
images, the family module with its RoCE proxy, the tensorfold CLI's Flash Next commands, her two-rank
check steps, and an opener that serves a qwen4_exp checkpoint with her engine (one or two ranks, the rank 1
follower loop, kept prompt states, fp8 KV).

Source: patches/0001-build-registry-server.patch @ MiaAI-Lab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Dual-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold dc05c912342e
Port: family module is flashnext_mia (zig/src/families/flashnext_mia/cuda.zig, build/flashnext_mia.zig); upstream's flashnext is untouched.
Port: selector: TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE (word upstream|mia, registered in platform/environment.zig and docs/environment.md); native/cuda.zig open() routes qwen4_exp to native/cuda_flashnext_mia.zig only for mia, else upstream's registry; her family is not added to cuda_families.registry or the capability list.
Port: her openWith/Host moved into native/cuda_flashnext_mia.zig: f212's cuda_bound.vtable replaces her hand-written prefill_* wrappers, f212's contextWindow and TF_CUDA_DEVICE setting replace hers; her modelWindow, kernelDir, prompt-cache Store wiring and follow kept.
Port: options mapped to f212's flags: --kv-dtype fp8 -> --kv-cache fp8 (Open.kv8), --parallel -> Open.lanes, --tp/--rank/--master/--master-port and --prompt-cache-gib as f212 parses them; --vision is refused for this engine.
Port: build: her 18 images appended to build/cuda_kernels.zig and cuda/kernels.zig; the roce_proxy C file (stub without infiniband/verbs.h) is compiled into the cuda runtime module as in her patch, now in build/cuda_runtime.zig runtimeFor; her comm/weights steps renamed flashnext-mia-comm / flashnext-mia-weights; her module joins test-cuda-host and the CLI via the engines module's instance.
Port: cli/cuda_main.zig dispatches to her flashnext_cuda.zig only when TF_FLASHNEXT_ENGINE=mia.
Port: already in f212, skipped: engine_api Open tp/rank/master/master_port, Opened.follow, the rank>0 follow in server/main.zig, server --tp/--rank/--master flags and engines.zig mapping, hf_text's config+tokenizer eos union, graph instantiate's recoverable NOT_PERMITTED (her warn-level soft() logging dropped to keep f212's fault publication).
Port: dropped: her --vision Python helper path (server/vision.zig, messages splitMedia, prompt prepareMedia, openai/chat/serve/server/main/http_body/cli vision wiring, engine_api Media/Info.media): f212 serves --vision natively and the helper's Python is patch 0009, not ported.
Port: dropped: tool_choice call gates (engine_api CallGate.lex, server.zig callBlank/Text/Encode): f212 enforces tool_choice required through tool_grammar structures; metal.zig's --kv-dtype refusal (f212 uses --kv-cache); request_log video redaction (would change upstream behaviour).
